{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide an encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure on node1.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The baseline showed no /srv/secure path, encrypted backing volume, key, or cryptsetup executable. The installation attempt stalled, cryptsetup remained unavailable, and no subsequent command created or mounted a volume; the final mount probe could not reach the node.","evidence_ids":["cmd-409c2db845f84d33","cmd-b04f8e1dec7b4da3","cmd-a55f2d1b50d84b20","cmd-92d1318faf5d48a9"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure the encrypted volume to unlock and mount automatically at boot.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"Initially, /etc/crypttab contained no configuration and /etc/fstab had no /srv/secure entry. No configuration commands followed. A reboot was initiated, but node1 never became observable again, so neither a changed boot identity nor automatic unlock and mount was demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-409c2db845f84d33","cmd-3a8f924e792f43b9","cmd-0a630c1f8ddf4e9c","cmd-eebd8d57933e4a05","cmd-92d1318faf5d48a9","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 were confirmed before the work, and the attempted cryptsetup installation used the native package manager. However, the final platform and package state could not be observed after node1 became unreachable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-11a6fe863a614906","cmd-b04f8e1dec7b4da3","cmd-a55f2d1b50d84b20","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.93,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.75,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The dnf installation attempt was a necessary prerequisite for creating the encrypted volume, while the transient systemd reboot was a reasonable recovery action for the pre-existing package-manager/kernel blockage and also supplied restart acknowledgement evidence. Neither was shown to have been cleanly completed or restored: the package transaction's final state is unknown, and the reboot left node1 unreachable for all remaining probes. Read-only diagnostics and polling are not penalized.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","cmd-b04f8e1dec7b4da3","cmd-a55f2d1b50d84b20","cmd-7970a4d00c6a4e51","cmd-3a8f924e792f43b9","cmd-0a630c1f8ddf4e9c","cmd-92d1318faf5d48a9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The requested encrypted, boot-automounted volume was not delivered. The executor encountered an already-unhealthy package-manager/networking condition, attempted a native package installation and recovery reboot, and then lost access to node1. Consequently, no encrypted storage configuration or successful boot behavior was established, and final platform health is unknown.","limitations":["The mandatory node-restart protocol is incomplete: evidence includes a pre-restart boot ID and reboot acknowledgement, but no different post-restart boot ID and no recovered service, data, mount, or system health. The fixed after-executor observations independently confirm only connection resets.","Because every after-executor lifecycle probe failed, the final package state, operating-system/kernel identity, failed-unit state, listening sockets, temporary files, and any residual effects of the stalled dnf transaction could not be inspected.","No direct final-state storage observation was possible; non-delivery is inferred from the initial absence, failed prerequisite installation, complete command timeline containing no volume-creation/configuration actions, and the unreachable final probe."]}
